 "specification": {
  "scope": "The SVCB RRset served for one DNS-AID agent name. The agent protocol of a record is its proto SvcParam when that member is present, even when it is empty, and otherwise the alpn tokens that are not transports (h2, h3, h2c, http/1.1). Each is a comma-separated string or a list of strings. A conforming RRset has exactly one record per agent protocol the publisher published, and no record names no protocol or two. Any other shape, a published list that is not strings, or a member file that is not strict JSON (a duplicate name, a NaN literal) is rrset-malformed. All fixtures are synthetic.",
  "sources": [
   "RFC 9460 Service Binding and Parameter Specification via the DNS (SVCB)",
   "IETF draft on DNS-based agent discovery, revision 02, section 3.1.1 example records",
   "IETF draft on DNS-based agent discovery, newer revision 00, section 3.1.1 and Table 1 (proto)"
  ],
  "status": "proposal of this repository, not a vendored upstream text",
  "verifierContract": "verifier <case file>: the last stdout line is one JSON object with `verdict` (valid or invalid) and `codes` (a set); exit 0 for valid, 1 for invalid."
 },
